00:18:39.270 --> 00:18:42.060
There's one final thing though
that I wanted to show you

00:18:42.060 --> 00:18:46.680
and that's the fact that
any agent that you build

00:18:46.680 --> 00:18:48.690
with Elastic Agent Builder,

00:18:48.690 --> 00:18:51.990
its operations are also
accessible via API.

00:18:51.990 --> 00:18:55.110
So, it's cool that we can come
in here into Agent Builder

00:18:55.110 --> 00:18:57.210
and chat with it
using this interface.

00:18:57.210 --> 00:19:01.320
But even cooler is all of
these functions are accessible

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:02.190
via API.

00:19:02.190 --> 00:19:03.360
So, if you want to integrate

00:19:03.360 --> 00:19:06.900
that into your existing
apps, it's easy to do.

00:19:06.900 --> 00:19:13.620
And so, for example, I can
propose a query like this.

00:19:13.620 --> 00:19:16.890
I could go look at the
documentation for the APIs

00:19:16.890 --> 00:19:19.320
for agents and I
encourage you to do that.

00:19:19.320 --> 00:19:22.050
But I wanted to show you how you
